  "area": "st-kitts-nevis",
  "method": "St. Kitts and Nevis (both islands, including the Narrows shoals between them). No government mooring list or marine-park site list is published online (the St Kitts Tourism Authority pages are a script-rendered shell with no site list, and the Sandy Point / Kittitian marine reserves publish no dive list), so the denominator rests on operator lists. Lists read: Pro Divers St Kitts, Kenneth's Dive Center (St Kitts), and Dive Nevis (the Oualie Beach operator, also trading as Scuba Safaris, whose own domain is dead; counted once). A site is counted when named on at least two of those independent operator lists; sites on one list are kept as excluded. Same-reef alternate names are merged (Monkey Shoals / Monkey Shoal Reef, Brimstone Shallows / Brimstone Reef, Coconut Tree Rocks / Coconut Reef). Everything listed is within recreational depth (130 ft / 40 m); Finger Reef is listed to 130 ft by one operator and 140 ft by the other, counted as recreational. Nevis is thinly covered by a single operator, so its sites mostly fall to the one-list exclusion. Counted 2026-10-14.",
